    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you; could you tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S030",
      "patient_response": "Hi, Dr. Smith. Yeah, it's nice to meet you too. Um, well, I guess I came in because... well, I just can't seem to shake this incredibly heavy feeling, you know? It really started settling in after we bought our house. I just keep feeling like I’ve completely let my family down by taking on this mortgage. It's a huge financial commitment, obviously, and I just look at the paperwork and think, what on earth was I thinking? \n\nI mean, I'm just a waiter. I took some classes in college years ago but I never finished my degree, and now I'm trying to support this massive loan on a server's wages. And the guilt about it is just... it's bleeding into absolutely everything I do. Like, every single small mistake I make at work lately—if I forget to bring a table their extra side of ranch dressing, or if I accidentally punch the wrong appetizer into the computer system—it just hits me so incredibly hard. It doesn't just feel like a simple error; it feels like it proves that I’m just totally useless. I'll just stand there in the back by the kitchen thinking that I deserve whatever bad things happen to me, because if I can't even get a basic lunch order right, how am I supposed to provide for my family and keep a roof over their heads? I just keep spiraling into this intense guilt over every little thing, and I can't seem to turn it off.",
