    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever felt this way for a period of time in the past, or is this the very first time you have experienced these feelings?",
      "targeted_symptom": "depressive_episode_duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, um, to be completely honest, it's not the very first time, no. But this particular stretch... it's been going on for a really long time. I mean, if I sit down and actually trace it back, I'd say these heavy, depressed, just overwhelming periods of guilt have been hanging over me for about a year and two months now. \n\nAnd I remember exactly when it started getting this bad, because it was right around the time we were finalizing the initial paperwork for the house, which was just over a year ago. It was supposed to be this exciting time, you know? My wife was looking at paint colors, and we were talking about where to put the furniture, but all I could feel was this crushing weight settling into my chest. And it just hasn't lifted since then. It's like, for the last fourteen months, I wake up and the very first thought in my head is about how I'm failing. And it just colors the whole day. Even on days when the restaurant isn't busy and things should be easy, I just carry this... this dark cloud of guilt around with me. So yeah, it's been about a year and two months of feeling exactly like this, just constantly.",
