    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "In the past fourteen months, have you had any periods of at least two months where your mood felt completely normal and you didn't experience these heavy feelings of guilt or sadness at all?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_2",
      "patient_response": "Well, um... no, not really. I mean, if I really sit and think about it, trying to find a solid block of time where I felt totally normal... I just can't. There definitely hasn't been a two-month stretch where I felt okay, that's for sure. \n\nI mean, sure, there might be a day here or there where the sun is shining, or maybe we have a really good dinner rush at the restaurant and I walk out with decent tips, and for a few hours, the weight doesn't feel quite as crushing. Maybe I'll even laugh at a joke one of the line cooks makes, you know? But it never lasts. It's like... it's like trying to hold a beach ball underwater. You can do it for a minute, but it always pops back up. \n\nFor most of this whole fourteen-month period, even when some days were a little lighter or I was distracted by something, I’ve just been weighed down by that empty, guilty feeling more often than not. It's just always there in the background, like static on a radio that you can't quite tune out. Even if I'm not actively spiraling about the mortgage in that exact second, the heaviness is still sitting right there on my chest. So, no, there hasn't been any real break from it. It's just been this constant, draining presence, day in and day out, for the vast majority of the time since we started all that paperwork.",
      "new_confirmed_symptoms": [
        "S024",
